articles.content_en:
When an energy emergency situation such as severe shortage of energy supply or interruption of supply occurs, the relevant people's government shall, within its authority, promptly initiate emergency response and may, in light of the actual circumstances and needs, take the following emergency response measures according to law:
(1) Release information on energy supply and demand and other relevant information;
(2) Implement emergency dispatch of energy production, transportation, and supply, or directly organize energy production, transportation, and supply;
(3) Requisition relevant energy products, energy reserve facilities, means of transport, and other materials for ensuring energy supply;
(4) Implement price intervention measures and emergency price measures;
(5) Organize the release of energy reserves in accordance with regulations;
(6) Organize and implement energy supply in accordance with the order of energy supply guarantee;
(7) Other necessary measures.
After the energy emergency situation is eliminated, the relevant people's government shall promptly terminate the implementation of emergency response measures.

The energy administration department and other relevant departments of people's governments at or above the county level shall, in accordance with their respective functions and duties, perform supervision and inspection duties according to law, and may take the following measures:
(1) Enter energy enterprises, dispatching agencies, energy market trading institutions, energy users and other entities to conduct on-site inspections;
(2) Inquire about persons related to the inspection matters, and require them to provide explanations on the relevant matters;
(3) Review and copy documents, materials, and electronic data related to the inspection matters;
(4) Other measures prescribed by laws and regulations.
The inspected entities and their relevant personnel shall cooperate with the supervision and inspection lawfully conducted by the energy administration department and other relevant departments, and shall not refuse or obstruct.
The energy administration department and other relevant departments and their staff members shall, according to law, have a duty of confidentiality regarding state secrets, trade secrets, personal privacy, and personal information learned during the supervision and inspection process.

If any of the following circumstances occurs in violation of the provisions of this Law, the energy administration department or other relevant departments of the people's government at or above the county level shall order correction and give a warning or a notice of criticism; if it refuses to correct, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed:
(1) An enterprise responsible for the supply of energy such as electricity, gas, and heat fails to disclose service standards, charging standards, and complaint channels, or fails to provide public inquiry services for energy users;
(2) An enterprise operating energy transmission pipeline network facilities fails to disclose information on the access and transmission capacity of energy transmission pipeline network facilities and their operation status in accordance with regulations;
(3) An energy enterprise fails to provide relevant data such as price cost in accordance with regulations;
(4) A relevant entity fails to submit relevant information to the energy administration department or other relevant departments in accordance with regulations.
